      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The integrand has the shape of an inverse trigonometric derivative, \\( \\frac{d}{dx} \\arcsin\\left(\\frac{x - 5}{7}\\right) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{49 - \\left(x - 5\\right)^{2}}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "antiderivative read from a derivative rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
